kwin 6.8: render nested sessions in software when the host takes no dmabufs

6.8 dropped QPainter compositing, so a kwin nested under a compositor that
renders with pixman (pixelflux on a host without a GPU) finds no render device
and cannot start: the host advertises no zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1, and kwin's own
software device needs /dev/udmabuf, which containers rarely get.

Let it render through llvmpipe anyway, and hand the frames to the host as
wl_shm buffers:

1. Where /dev/udmabuf can't be opened, a software render device is created on
   demand whose buffers are plain memfds. llvmpipe imports a dmabuf by mapping
   it, so it takes the memfd as a linear dmabuf just the same, and renders into
   it with no copies. Nothing outside this process can import those buffers,
   so the device has no device id, is never offered to clients for dmabufs
   (they share over wl_shm, as with 6.7's QPainter), and screencasts stream it
   as memfds.

2. Buffers from the udmabuf allocator expose their memfd as shm attributes,
   sized to the picture without the allocator's padding.

3. The Wayland backend falls back to the software device when the host takes
   dmabufs from no device kwin can use and there is no GPU to render on, and
   then presents through wl_shm in linear ARGB8888/XRGB8888, which every
   compositor accepts. With a GPU nothing changes.

Only adds functions to exported classes, so the library stays compatible with
the stock kwin_wayland executable and plugins of the same version.

Applies to kwin 6.8.x (verified against v6.8.0).

